1
00:04:31,111 --> 00:04:37,111
Can a great man be a good man?

2
00:09:02,222 --> 00:09:08,222
Steve Jobs is a drama, history film directed by Danny Boyle.

3
00:13:33,333 --> 00:13:39,333
Set backstage at three iconic product launches and ending in 1998 with the unveiling of the iMac, Steve Jobs takes us behind
the scenes of the digital revolution to paint an intimate portrait of the brilliant man at its epicenter.

4
00:18:04,444 --> 00:18:10,444
Steve Jobs, played by Michael Fassbender.

5
00:22:35,555 --> 00:22:41,555
Joanna Hoffman, played by Kate Winslet.

6
00:27:06,666 --> 00:27:12,666
Steve Wozniak, played by Seth Rogen.

7
00:31:37,777 --> 00:31:43,777
John Sculley, played by Jeff Daniels.

8
00:36:08,888 --> 00:36:14,888
Andy Hertzfeld, played by Michael Stuhlbarg.

9
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:46,000
Chrisann Brennan, played by Katherine Waterston.

10
00:45:11,111 --> 00:45:17,111
Steve Jobs is a 2015 biographical drama film directed by
Danny Boyle and written by Aaron Sorkin.

11
00:49:42,222 --> 00:49:48,222
A British-American co-production, it was adapted from the 2011 biography
by Walter Isaacson and interviews conducted by Sorkin.

12
00:54:13,333 --> 00:54:19,333
The film covers fourteen years in the life of Apple Inc.

13
00:58:44,444 --> 00:58:50,444
co-founder Steve Jobs, specifically ahead of three press conferences he gave during that time: the formal unveiling of the Macintosh 128K on
January 24, 1984; the unveiling of the NeXT Computer on October 12, 1988; and the unveiling of the iMac G3 on May 6, 1998.

14
01:03:15,555 --> 01:03:21,555
Jobs is portrayed by Michael Fassbender, with Kate Winslet as Joanna Hoffman, Seth Rogen
as Steve Wozniak, and Jeff Daniels as John Sculley in supporting roles.

15
01:07:46,666 --> 01:07:52,666
Development began in 2011 after the rights to Isaacson's book were acquired.

16
01:12:17,777 --> 01:12:23,777
Filming began in January 2015.

17
01:16:48,888 --> 01:16:54,888
A variety of actors were considered and cast before
Fassbender eventually took the role.

18
01:21:20,000 --> 01:21:26,000
Editing was extensive on the project, with editor Elliot
Graham starting while the film was still shooting.

19
01:25:51,111 --> 01:25:57,111
Daniel Pemberton served as composer, with a focus on dividing
the score into three distinguishable sections.

20
01:30:22,222 --> 01:30:28,222
Steve Jobs premiered at the 2015 Telluride Film Festival on September 5, 2015, and began
a limited release in New York City and Los Angeles on October 9, 2015.

21
01:34:53,333 --> 01:34:59,333
It opened nationwide in the United States on October 23, 2015, to widespread critical acclaim, with Boyle's direction, visual style, Sorkin's
screenplay, musical score, cinematography, editing and the acting of Fassbender, Winslet, Rogen and Daniels garnering unanimous acclaim.

22
01:39:24,444 --> 01:39:30,444
However, it was a financial disappointment, grossing only $34.4
million worldwide against a budget of $30 million.

23
01:43:55,555 --> 01:44:01,555
People close to Jobs such as Steve Wozniak and John Sculley praised the
performances, but the film also received criticism for historical inaccuracy.

24
01:48:26,666 --> 01:48:32,666
Steve Jobs was nominated for Best Actor (Fassbender) and Best Supporting Actress
(Winslet) at the 88th Academy Awards, and received numerous other accolades.

25
01:52:57,777 --> 01:53:03,777
The film explores themes of computer, biography, based on true
story, father daughter relationship, wonder.

26
01:57:28,888 --> 01:57:34,888
The tone is emotional and intense.
